From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:20:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 045/105] gdn: chain-parallel verify conv1d
 (SGLANG_GDN_CONV_CHAIN_PARALLEL)

The target-verify causal conv1d walks the T draft tokens of a sequence
serially inside one CTA, so the 16-token verify costs ~2.5x the 4-token
one purely from loop length (36 calls/step, 261us at T=16 vs 106us at
T=4).

With topk=1 chain speculation the draft tokens are a straight line, so
out[t] = act(bias + sum_k w[k]*x[t-(W-1)+k]) is independent per position
(x[<0] from the incoming conv state). The new
_causal_conv1d_update_chain_kernel spreads the tokens over a third grid
axis of BLOCK_T-wide tiles while keeping the per-output accumulation
order, the fp32 accumulator, the SiLU and the store rounding of the
serial kernel unchanged.

The incoming conv state is read and rolled forward by the tile-0 CTA
only (BLOCK_T >= width-1 guarantees it owns every output whose window
reaches before token 0), so there is a single writer and no race.

Off by default; the eagle tree path (topk>1), num_accept_tokens rolling,
circular cache_seqlens, seqlen==1 decode, width outside 2..4 and out=
aliasing x all keep the old kernel.

Measured on RTX PRO 6000 (bs=1, dim=10240, width=4, SAVE_INTERMEDIATE),
kernel self time: T=16 4.24us -> 2.15us (1.97x), T=4 1.64 -> 1.62us.
84/84 torch.equal cases pass on outputs, conv state and intermediate
window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
